The attached image illustrates the transient inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11 nanoparticles at the injection site over time. Panel A shows the kinetics of various inflammatory cell types, revealing a predominant and sustained recruitment of Mac-2+ macrophages, antigen-presenting cells (MHCII+), and Ly6C+ monocytes peaking around day 2, while neutrophils show an earlier, sharper, and more transient increase. Panel B, through confocal microscopy, visually confirms the intracellular presence of Nano-11 (red) within MHCII+, Ly6C+, and Mac-2+ cells (green) at different time points, demonstrating efficient phagocytosis by these immune cells in vivo and supporting Nano-11's ability to target antigen-presenting cells at the site of injection.